\pard\nowidctlpar\b\f0\fs28 HiQNet\b0\fs20\par
\par
Driver provides ability to set and monitor parameters from HiQnet compatible devices. Supports up to 16 devices simultaneously, with up to 20 parameters per device.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Configuration\b0\fs20\par
\par
\b Global Settings\par
\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Total Device Count\b0  \emdash  Number of HiQNet devices to control (1\endash 16).\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b Advanced Settings\par
\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Protocol Version\b0  \emdash  HiQNet protocol version. Use \b 02\b0  for modern HiQNet-compatible devices. Use \b 01\b0  only for dbx ZonePro devices.\par
\par
\b Source Node Address\b0  \emdash  HiQNet node address assigned to this driver (default: 52). Must be unique on the network and must not conflict with Audio Architect\rquote s HiQNet address.\par
\par
\b Polling Interval (Seconds)\b0  \emdash  Keep-alive send interval in seconds (default: 8). Must be less than the device\rquote s 10-second KAP timeout.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b Per-Device Settings\b0  (configured for each device 1\endash 16)\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Device Name\b0  \emdash  Friendly name used in RTI variable and event labels.\par
\par
\b IP / Hostname\b0  \emdash  IP address or hostname of the HiQNet device.\par
\par
\b HiQNet Address\b0  \emdash  The device\rquote s HiQNet network address, as shown in Audio Architect.\par
\par
\b HiQNet Virtual Device\b0  \emdash  The device\rquote s virtual device number, as shown in Audio Architect (typically 0).\par
\par
\b Parameter Count\b0  \emdash  Number of parameters to control or monitor on this device (1\endash 20).\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b Per-Parameter Settings\b0  (configured for each parameter per device)\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Name\b0  \emdash  Friendly name used in RTI variable labels.\par
\par
\b Object Address\b0  \emdash  The parameter\rquote s object address as shown in Audio Architect, in dot-separated decimal format (e.g., \b 15.22.7\b0 ).\par
\par
\b Parameter ID\b0  \emdash  The parameter ID as shown in Audio Architect.\par
\par
\b Allow Set\b0  \emdash  Enables sending values to the device for this parameter.\par
\par
\b Set Method\b0  (when Allow Set is enabled) \emdash  \b Set (typed)\b0  sends a raw typed value. \b Set % (1.15 fixed point)\b0  encodes the value as a 1.15 fixed-point percentage.\par
\par
\b Data Type\b0  (when Set Method is \ldblquote Set typed\rdblquote ) \emdash  HiQNet data type of the value being sent: BYTE, UBYTE, WORD, UWORD, LONG, ULONG, FLOAT32, FLOAT64, LONG64, or ULONG64.\par
\par
\b Enable Subscribe\b0  \emdash  Subscribes to push updates for this parameter from the device.\par
\par
\b Variable Type\b0  (when Enable Subscribe is enabled) \emdash  RTI variable type used to represent the received value: \b Boolean\b0 , \b Integer\b0 , or \b String\b0 . When Data Type is FLOAT32 or FLOAT64 and Variable Type is Integer, the received float is multiplied by 100 and rounded before storage (e.g., 0.75 \rarrow  75).\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b\fs24 Variables\b0\fs20\par
\par
Variables are created per device (N = device number, 1\endash 16) and per parameter (P = parameter number, 1\endash 20). Category and variable labels use the configured device and parameter names.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Connected\i N\i0\b0  (Boolean) \emdash  True when device N is connected; false when disconnected.\par
\par
\b ParameterBoolValue\i N\i0 _\i P\i0\b0  (Boolean) \emdash  Current value of parameter P on device N, for parameters with Variable Type = Boolean.\par
\par
\b ParameterIntValue\i N\i0 _\i P\i0\b0  (Integer) \emdash  Current value of parameter P on device N, for parameters with Variable Type = Integer.\par
\par
\b ParameterStringValue\i N\i0 _\i P\i0\b0  (String) \emdash  Current value of parameter P on device N, for parameters with Variable Type = String.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b\fs24 Functions\b0\fs20\par
\par
Functions are created per device (N = device number, 1\endash 16) and per parameter (P = parameter number, 1\endash 20). Category labels use the configured device name.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Set \i [Parameter Name]\i0  Value\b0  \emdash  Sends the specified hex string value to parameter P on device N. Only available for parameters with Allow Set enabled. The value is sent using the configured Set Method and Data Type for that parameter.\par
\par
\b Dump Device Info\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Queries standard HiQnet attributes (IDs 0x0001\endash 0x0006) on device N and logs the response to the trace log. Intended for debugging and device discovery.\par
\par
\b Dump VD List\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Broadcasts a GetVDList request and logs the response to the trace log. Intended for debugging.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b\fs24 Events\b0\fs20\par
\par
Events are fired per device (N = device number, 1\endash 16).\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\b Connected\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Fired when device N successfully connects and completes initialization.\par
\par
\b Disconnected\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Fired when device N loses its connection after previously being connected.\par
\par
\b Initialized\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Fired when device N is instantiated during driver startup.\par
\par
\b ConnectionFailed\i N\i0\b0  \emdash  Fired when a TCP connection attempt to device N fails.\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\b\fs24 Revision History\b0\fs20\par
\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx450 1.0:\tab Original release of the driver (partially complete)\par
2.0:\tab Finish implementation of HiQNet protocol, many bug fixes\par
2.2:\tab Hello session refusal; correct subscribe/unsubscribe lifecycle; percent push notification handling (ParamSetPercent, ParamSubscribePercent); fix FLOAT32/FLOAT64 value decoding; add Dump Device Info and Dump VD List debug commands\par
}
